From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kaonic <dev@beechat.network>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 15:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gpio: keep devicetree bias flags when requesting a GPIO

gpio-uclass parses GPIO_PULL_UP / GPIO_PULL_DOWN out of a `gpios` property,
and drivers that implement set_flags act on them. But gpio_request_tail()
masks the parsed flags with GPIOD_MASK_DIR, which covers only the direction
bits, so the bias is discarded between being read and being applied.

GPIOD_MASK_PULL already exists for these bits; preserve it too.

Signed-off-by: Kaonic <dev@beechat.network>
---
 drivers/gpio/gpio-uclass.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpio/gpio-uclass.c b/drivers/gpio/gpio-uclass.c
--- a/drivers/gpio/gpio-uclass.c
+++ b/drivers/gpio/gpio-uclass.c
@@ -1116,9 +1116,10 @@
 		goto err;
 	}
 
-	/* Keep any direction flags provided by the devicetree */
+	/* Keep any direction and bias flags provided by the devicetree */
 	ret = dm_gpio_set_dir_flags(desc,
-				    flags | (desc->flags & GPIOD_MASK_DIR));
+				    flags | (desc->flags &
+				     (GPIOD_MASK_DIR | GPIOD_MASK_PULL)));
 	if (ret) {
 		debug("%s: dm_gpio_set_dir failed\n", __func__);
 		goto err;
 	}
